# Internal working documents: adversarial review reports, per-worker notes, and
# the routing/draft/validation artifacts of the hardening rounds. These are
# development process material, not part of what the project publishes, and they
# name weaknesses in current code. They live here so they stay out of every
# remote; see docs/ for the published set.
/.internal-docs/

# The working instructions are process material by the same rule: the push
# manual, the local gate, the standing design policies, and notes about this
# machine. They are not explanation or usage, so they do not belong in the
# published tree. The file stays in the working tree -- it has to, that is how
# it is read -- and is tracked on the `internal` branch only, the same way
# /.internal-docs/ is. Untracked here with `git rm --cached`, because adding a
# line to this file does not untrack something git already tracks.
#
# This file differs by branch by design: these two lines are ACTIVE here and
# commented out on `internal`, because git cannot track an ignored path. Do not
# cherry-pick a commit touching this file between the two -- it carries neither
# guarded path, so the pre-push hook has nothing to refuse.
/CLAUDE.md
